.TH WATCH 1 "October 2026" "watch 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
watch \- terminal client to search, stream and download anime
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B watch
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ query ]
.br
.B watch
.RI [ query ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B watch
searches the enabled anime providers, presents matching titles and episodes, resolves available streams, and opens the selected media with a supported player. It can also download episodes and maintain a compatible watch-history file.
.PP
The active Rust implementation is developed on the
.B main
branch. Watch is a fork of pystardust/ani-cli; see the repository README for attribution.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show command help.
.TP
.BR -V ", " --version
Show the installed version.
.TP
.BR -c ", " --continue
Continue from watch history.
.TP
.BR -d ", " --download
Download selected episode(s) instead of playing them.
.TP
.BR -D ", " --delete
Delete watch history.
.TP
.BR -l ", " --logview
Show available system log entries.
.TP
.BR -s ", " --syncplay
Use Syncplay.
.TP
.BR -S ", " --select-nth " " N
Select the one-based item index.
.TP
.BR -q ", " --quality " " QUALITY
Select a quality such as
.B best
,
.B worst
or
.B 720p
.
.TP
.B --language LANGUAGE
Filter catalog and history choices by language. English accepts english, en, ingles, or inglés. Spanish accepts spanish, es, espanol, or español. Matching is case-insensitive. This filters source language; use --dub to request dubbed audio.
.TP
.BR -v ", " --vlc
Use VLC.
.TP
.BR -e ", " --episode " " RANGE
Select episode numbers or ranges, for example
.B 5-6
,
.B "1 3 5"
,
.B 0
(first episode), or
.B -1
(last episode).
.TP
.B --range RANGE
Alias for
.BR --episode .
.TP
.B --dub
Select dubbed audio when available.
.TP
.B --rofi
Use Rofi for selection.
.TP
.B --dmenu
Use dmenu for selection.
.TP
.B --skip
Skip the intro when the selected player supports ani-skip.
.TP
.B --inline, --here
Ask MPV to render video inside the terminal. The MPV output driver and terminal must support the same graphics protocol. An available MPV driver does not prove that the terminal supports it; use regular external playback if no frames appear.
.TP
.B --no-detach
Keep playback attached to the terminal.
.TP
.B --exit-after-play
Exit after playback and return the player status.
.TP
.B -N, --nextep-countdown
Show the next-episode countdown before continuing into search/playback.
.TP
.B -U, --update
Update the Rust installation from the selected Git branch using Cargo.
.SH INTERACTIVE CONTROLS
A single anime result or single available episode is selected automatically and reported to the user.
.PP
The built-in numbered menu shows 15 entries per page. In a directly attached terminal, use the left and right arrow keys to change pages; the menu redraws in place. If the console is unavailable, the line-based menu accepts
.B n
for the next page or
.B p
for the previous page. Selection numbers refer to the full list.
.PP
Press
.B Backspace
with an empty selection to return to the previous step. Backspace from anime results returns to the search prompt. Press
.B q
or
.B Esc
to cancel and exit successfully. When
.B fzf
is used, Backspace is reserved for navigating back instead of editing its filter.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ANI_CLI_DEFAULT_SOURCE
Default source: search, history, or nextep.
.TP
.B ANI_CLI_MODE
Default audio mode: sub or dub.
.TP
.B ANI_CLI_QUALITY
Default quality, such as best, worst, 1080p or 720p.
.TP
.B ANI_CLI_EXACT
Set to 1 to require an exact normalized title match.
.TP
.B ANI_CLI_MENU
Default menu backend: fzf, rofi or dmenu.
.TP
.B ANI_CLI_MENU_FLAGS
Additional arguments for the selected external menu.
.TP
.B ANI_CLI_PLAYER
Select mpv, vlc, syncplay, iina, or a custom player executable.
.TP
.B ANI_CLI_PLAYER_FLAGS
Additional player/downloader arguments.
.TP
.B ANI_CLI_NO_DETACH
Set to 1 to keep the player attached to the terminal.
.TP
.B ANI_CLI_EXIT_AFTER_PLAY
Set to 1 to return the player exit status after playback.
.TP
.B ANI_CLI_SKIP_INTRO
Set to 1 to enable intro skipping where supported.
.TP
.B ANI_CLI_DOWNLOAD_DIR
Directory for downloaded episodes.
.TP
.B ANI_CLI_HIST_DIR
Directory containing the compatible ani-hsts history file.
.TP
.B ANI_CLI_LOG
Set to 0 to disable system logger records.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
Rust 1.85 or newer is required to build from source. Playback needs an installed external media player such as MPV or VLC. Android playback uses MPV-Android by default; see the Watch Android / Termux guide. Downloads use yt-dlp when available and FFmpeg as the fallback; FFmpeg is also required to mux separate audio and video renditions. Syncplay and ani-skip are optional.
.SH FILES
The history file is resolved using the platform-specific data directory or
.BR ANI_CLI_HIST_DIR .
Legacy numeric-ID history entries are backed up to a
.B .v4
file during migration.
.SH BUGS
The client depends on third-party provider markup, streaming hosts and external media tools. Their behavior can change independently of this program.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cargo (1),
.BR mpv (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR yt-dlp (1)
